<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alcazaba of Almería</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">10th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Alcazaba of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almeria">Almería</a> is a fortified complex on a hill above Almería in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, founded under the Córdoban <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-iii">Abd al-Rahman III</a> in the 10th century. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> ruler al-Mutasim enlarged it in the 11th century with palaces and gardens, and after the Christian conquest of 1489 the Catholic Monarchs added a castle. It is the second-largest Muslim fortress in Spain, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alhambra">Alhambra</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alcazaba-of-almeria.jpg" alt="Alcazaba of Almería" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ANE · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alcazaba_de_Almer%C3%ADa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
